      "label": "percentage discount rounds half away from zero: 1.05 * 0.5 % = 0.00525 -> 0.01, not banker's 0.00",
      "traps": [
        "numeric-rounding"
      ],
      "reasoning": "T-SQL ROUND(@UnitPrice * @HighestDiscountPercentage / 100.0, 2) rounds half away from zero; PostgreSQL round(numeric,2) must do the same, not round-half-to-even. UnitPrice 1.05 ends in 5 and the product 0.00525 is the half-way-ish case a banker's-rounding conversion would mishandle.",
